          <h2 class="text-2xl font-black text-white mb-4">The Bottom Line</h2>
          <p class="text-gray-300 leading-relaxed mb-4">
            Fruity Pebbles protein powder is better than its branding suggests. The ISO100 version is a genuine whey isolate with 25 g of protein, about 120 calories and roughly 1 g of sugar per scoop, and the Cocoa Pebbles and Birthday Cake flavors share the same label. If you want a fun flavor that does not compromise your macros, it is one of the easiest recommendations on the shelf.
          </p>
          <p class="text-gray-300 leading-relaxed mb-4">
            Buy the 20-serving tub first, move to the 5 lb tub if you like it, and ignore the mass gainer unless you truly need the calories. If you want a creamier fruity cereal shake, Ghost Whey Trix Cereal Milk is the alternative, and if you would rather avoid sweeteners and colors altogether, an unflavored isolate is the better buy.
